{"getBaseConditions() treats both auth and filter conditions as truthy values; since auth conditions always return a Prisma.Sql (including 1=0), verify the intended semantics when filters are absent and auth resolves to NOTHING_CONDITION, and ensure callers don't accidentally treat 1=0 as no condition rather than deny all.": 0.283639520406723, "SQL injection / authorization scope: The new implementation constructs raw SQL conditions for authorization and filtering. While template interpolation via Prisma.sql should parameterize values, pay extra attention to ANY(${array}) bindings and any future changes that might interpolate untrusted strings/identifiers. Also re-validate that the OR-combination of team-scope and user-scope predicates cannot broaden access beyond the intended org/team membership rules.": 0.1973687708377838, "Validate that using ANY(${someNumberArray}) inside Prisma.sql binds as a proper Postgres int[] (and not e.g. JSON/text), otherwise the ANY() predicates may behave incorrectly or error. Consider whether explicit casting or Prisma.join is needed depending on Prisma/PG behavior.": 0.3786378800868988, "Direct equality checks against Prisma.sql objects can be brittle if Prisma changes SQL formatting/parentheses/whitespace or parameter ordering. Consider asserting on behavior (query results) or normalizing the SQL representation rather than strict object equality for complex OR/AND conditions.": 0.305781751871109}